From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 07:11:10 -0644
Subject: [PATCH] clk: samsung: zumapro: Keep the HSI0 USI2 and USI3 clocks on

The gates of USI2 and USI3 in the HSI0 block (the bus, function and
source clock of each) are writable and in manual mode, and nothing holds
them while the SPI controllers behind them are idle. A register access
to the USI in the first microseconds after its gates are opened never
returns: the CPU sits in the access, takes no tick and answers no IPI.

The USI driver does that in its noirq resume (clk_bulk_prepare_enable(),
then USI_CON read and written), and so on the Pixel 9a a sleep now and
then never woke. Two such hangs were caught with the device callback
trace events on. In the first, at the 41st sleep of a boot, the suspend
task's last event is device_pm_callback_start for the USI at 111d00c0
(USI2, the touchscreen's SPI), with no end. In the second, on a kernel
that kept only the two bus clocks on, USI2's callback returns and the
last event is the start of USI3's, at 111e00c0, at the 227th sleep. The
USIs resumed before them, in PERIC0 and PERIC1, have read-only gates,
and so has USI4 in HSI0.

It reproduces awake in under a second. A test module that repeats the
driver's sequence on USI3 (clocks on, USI_CON read and written, 1 us,
clocks off), with the bus clock already on and only the function clock
switched, hung the SoC within its first thousand rounds, twice of twice,
until the watchdog reset it. With 10 us between the clocks and the
access, two million rounds passed, and so did two million rounds that
switched the clocks and touched no register.

Mark the six gates critical, as the PERIC0 and HSI2 GPIO gates are, so
the clock framework never closes them. With that, on the published tree
with nothing else added, two million rounds of the same module passed on
each USI with the gates never closed. Before it, with a module holding
the two USIs' clocks on, 300 of 300 sleeps of 60 s woke on the build
that had hung at the 70th and the 41st.

Signed-off-by: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/clk/samsung/clk-zumapro.c | 19 +++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/samsung/clk-zumapro.c b/drivers/clk/samsung/clk-zumapro.c
index d813b970b..56dd307be 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/samsung/clk-zumapro.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/samsung/clk-zumapro.c
@@ -664,21 +664,28 @@ static const struct samsung_div_clock hsi0_dividers[] __initconst = {
 	      0x1824, 0, 4, 0, CLK_DIVIDER_READ_ONLY),
 };
 
+/*
+ * The USI2 and USI3 gates are in manual mode and stay on. A register access
+ * in the first microseconds after one of them is opened never returns, and
+ * the USI driver's resume and the SPI controllers' runtime PM open them
+ * right before theirs: on the Pixel 9a that hung the noirq resume now and
+ * then.
+ */
 static const struct samsung_gate_clock hsi0_gates[] __initconst = {
 	GATE(CLK_GOUT_HSI0_USI2_SOURCE, "zumapro_gout_hsi0_usi2_source",
 	     "zumapro_mout_hsi0_usi2_local",
-	     0x2120, 21, CLK_IGNORE_UNUSED, 0),
+	     0x2120, 21, CLK_IS_CRITICAL, 0),
 	GATE(CLK_GOUT_HSI0_USI2_IP, "zumapro_gout_hsi0_usi2_ip", "zumapro_dout_hsi0_usi2",
-	     0x20fc, 21, CLK_IGNORE_UNUSED | CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT, 0),
+	     0x20fc, 21, CLK_IS_CRITICAL | CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT, 0),
 	GATE(CLK_GOUT_HSI0_USI2_PCLK, "zumapro_gout_hsi0_usi2_pclk", "zumapro_mout_hsi0_noc_local",
-	     0x2100, 21, CLK_IGNORE_UNUSED, 0),
+	     0x2100, 21, CLK_IS_CRITICAL, 0),
 	GATE(CLK_GOUT_HSI0_USI3_SOURCE, "zumapro_gout_hsi0_usi3_source",
 	     "zumapro_mout_hsi0_usi3_local",
-	     0x2124, 21, CLK_IGNORE_UNUSED | CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT, 0),
+	     0x2124, 21, CLK_IS_CRITICAL | CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT, 0),
 	GATE(CLK_GOUT_HSI0_USI3_IP, "zumapro_gout_hsi0_usi3_ip", "zumapro_dout_hsi0_usi3",
-	     0x2104, 21, CLK_IGNORE_UNUSED | CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT, 0),
+	     0x2104, 21, CLK_IS_CRITICAL | CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT, 0),
 	GATE(CLK_GOUT_HSI0_USI3_PCLK, "zumapro_gout_hsi0_usi3_pclk", "zumapro_mout_hsi0_noc_local",
-	     0x2108, 21, CLK_IGNORE_UNUSED, 0),
+	     0x2108, 21, CLK_IS_CRITICAL, 0),
 };
 
 /*
